    "text": "Can the write-to-read-only check and unknown-register check overlap?",
    "default": "Register number >= 8 gives 3; registers 0,4,5,6,7 give 5 on write.",
    "reason": "The two sets do not overlap, so this is a confirmation.",
    "answer": "No, they cannot overlap. The spec checks register number first: READ/WRITE with P0 > 7 is refused with code 3. The code 5 rule applies only to WRITE to registers 0 or 4..7, all of which are <= 7 and so pass the code 3 check. A write to a given register number therefore gets either code 3 or code 5, never both. The proposed default matches this: register number >= 8 gives 3; writes to 0, 4, 5, 6, 7 give 5. The spec does not state the ordering explicitly, but the two conditions are disjoint by their definitions, so no precedence rule is needed.",
